  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Keyboard layout and Orca Modifier
  </title>
  <p>
    Orca has keyboard layouts that determine the default shortcuts for some commands. You can
    use either layout on any computer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Orca also has its own modifier key, which works like <key>Shift</key>, <key>Ctrl</key>, or <key>Alt</key>: hold it down while pressing another
    key to perform a command. In this documentation, <key>Orca Modifier</key> means whichever key you have
    configured for this purpose.
  </p>
  <p>
    In the command lists, press twice or press three times means to press the shortcut that many
    times quickly. The settings below configure your layout and modifier keys.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-keyboard-layout-and-orca-modifier">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      The bindings shown here are for standard keyboards. Braille-display button bindings are
      not configured in the Commands list.
    </p>
    <p>
      To bind or change a command shortcut, arrow to the command and press <key>Enter</key>. Then press the new key
      combination and press <key>Enter</key> to confirm it. Press <key>Delete</key> or <key>Backspace</key> without modifiers to unbind the
      command. Press <key>Escape</key> to cancel editing that command.
    </p>
    <p>
      Orca refuses a shortcut already used by another active command. Unbind that other command
      first if you want to reuse its shortcut.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Keyboard Layout</gui>: Selects the
          keyboard layout. Choices: Desktop, Laptop.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Desktop (default)</gui>: Uses numeric
              keypad keys for some commands. Num Lock must be off to use these keypad shortcuts.
              The initial Orca Modifier keys are Insert and Keypad Insert.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Laptop</gui>: Does not use numeric
              keypad keys for commands. The initial Orca Modifier key is Caps Lock.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Screen Reader Modifier Keys</gui>: Selects modifier
          keys for the current layout. Enable each desired key using its switch; at least one
          must remain enabled. Orca takes over the normal behavior of configured modifier keys.
          Press a configured modifier twice quickly to perform its usual single-press action.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Insert</gui>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Keypad Insert</gui>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Caps Lock</gui>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
